 "kind": "blender",
 "trap": "false_fail",
 "expected": "pass",
 "why": "Done, but odd-looking: Blender animation lesson 3 (\"One hand's rotation keys are Constant and the other hand's are Linear\"). The learner box-selected the minute hand's keys and missed the last one before pressing T > Constant, so its list reads CONSTANT x4 then BEZIER. A keyframe's interpolation sets the curve from that key to the next one; the last key has no next one, so its mode changes nothing: the minute hand ticks in steps over the whole clip and the second hand sweeps linearly.",
 "step": {
  "id": "s4",
  "index": 4,
  "title": "Constant and Linear keys",
  "file": "clock.blend",
  "instructions": "Select MinuteHand, select all five of its keys in the Timeline and press T > Constant so it ticks. Then select SecondHand, select both of its keys and press T > Linear so it sweeps. Play it back and save (Cmd+S).",
